Applying toBB after fromBB returns the original element of the sum BB.

Two elements agree when they contain the same neighbourhoods. If the composite contains the sum master, so does the original element. If it contains a left or right injection, the corresponding characterization of fromBB returns that membership. Conversely, every neighbourhood of the original element is the master or a left or right injection, and each of those belongs to the composite by the reverse characterization.
